WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.106 --> 00:00:01.752
- I'm Allis Markham, this is Prey,

00:00:01.752 --> 00:00:05.404
my taxidermy studio in
downtown Los Angeles.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.517
Everything I work on
dies of natural causes.

00:00:08.517 --> 00:00:12.357
I love animals and I love
making them last forever.

00:00:12.357 --> 00:00:14.551
So today, we're going to teach vegans

00:00:14.551 --> 00:00:18.044
how to mount ducklings as taxidermy.

00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:22.722
Vegans Try Taxidermy

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.611
- I'm Sigi, I've been vegan since moving

00:00:24.611 --> 00:00:26.318
to L.A. about five years ago.

00:00:26.318 --> 00:00:28.918
- I'm Nick, I've been
vegetarian for about 10 years

00:00:28.918 --> 00:00:30.097
and vegan for six months.

00:00:30.097 --> 00:00:31.945
- My name's Morgan and I've been vegan

00:00:31.945 --> 00:00:33.408
for about a year and a half.

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:34.444
- I'm very nervous.

00:00:34.444 --> 00:00:35.257
- Pretty nervous.

00:00:35.257 --> 00:00:38.833
- I'm feeling embarrassed
at how nervous I am.

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:40.458
- It's just kind of creepy.

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:44.811
- I'm imagining the worst
possible scenarios in here.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.229
Oh, man, it's uncomfortable (laughs).

00:00:47.229 --> 00:00:48.793
- Bag of ducklings.

00:00:48.793 --> 00:00:53.793
These are going to be your specimens.

00:00:55.159 --> 00:00:56.107
Alright.

00:00:56.107 --> 00:00:58.159
So we're going to take
this in three parts today.

00:00:58.159 --> 00:01:00.232
First, we're going to be kind of

00:01:00.232 --> 00:01:02.174
deconstructing our ducklings.

00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:03.909
We're going to be taking
them apart, skinning them.

00:01:03.909 --> 00:01:06.024
Then, we're going to
be cleaning that skin,

00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:08.868
so it's not attractive
to like pests and things.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.207
And then we're essentially going to be

00:01:10.207 --> 00:01:11.954
putting them back together

00:01:11.954 --> 00:01:13.458
to look like little cute ducklings.

00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:15.022
Deconstructing

00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:16.952
Warning: this part is graphic

00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:19.443
So do you want to watch
me make my first incision

00:01:19.443 --> 00:01:20.892
and then I'm going to
ask you to make yours.

00:01:21.062 --> 00:01:22.154
I start at the top of the chest

00:01:22.154 --> 00:01:24.683
and this scalpel is super sharp,

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.776
so I can just go real lightly.

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:28.137
- I just realized, I'm going to take

00:01:28.137 --> 00:01:29.052
off my watch for this.

00:01:29.052 --> 00:01:29.681
- Okay.

00:01:29.681 --> 00:01:31.459
Just slide it down.

00:01:34.736 --> 00:01:35.161
Perfect.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.339
- This is so insane.

00:01:36.339 --> 00:01:38.066
- I got a little bit
light headed for a second.

00:01:38.066 --> 00:01:40.890
- [Allis] Well, just remember,
it can't get much worse

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.353
because they're already dead.

00:01:42.353 --> 00:01:43.999
- Apparently I'm good at this

00:01:43.999 --> 00:01:48.999
which is a little bit frightening
but I guess you never know

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:51.597
what your talents are until you try them.

00:01:51.597 --> 00:01:53.019
- [Allis] Well, the good news is we're

00:01:53.019 --> 00:01:55.303
about to cut the bodies off.

00:01:55.303 --> 00:01:56.814
The bad news is we're
not quite done with them.

00:01:56.814 --> 00:02:01.325
I'm gonna have you go
ahead and snip the neck

00:02:01.325 --> 00:02:03.999
right about there off.

00:02:03.999 --> 00:02:05.486
- I don't know if I can watch this.

00:02:08.348 --> 00:02:10.302
One, two, three.

00:02:10.302 --> 00:02:12.922
(group groans)

00:02:12.922 --> 00:02:14.893
- How do you remove some things,

00:02:14.893 --> 00:02:18.489
innards from its neck
in a respectable way,

00:02:18.489 --> 00:02:19.525
like in a respectable way?

00:02:19.525 --> 00:02:22.004
So that I'm not... (laughs).

00:02:22.004 --> 00:02:24.075
- [Allis] I don't know,
maybe just cross yourself,

00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:25.348
I'm not sure.

00:02:25.348 --> 00:02:27.298
- No, Jesus doesn't
need to come into this.

00:02:27.945 --> 00:02:31.339
- Mmm, oh, weird, oh, man,
that felt weird inside of me.

00:02:31.339 --> 00:02:33.243
- Go big or go home.

00:02:35.181 --> 00:02:37.794
- [Allis] That was good,
good job, you guys.

00:02:37.794 --> 00:02:40.698
- I'm definitely glad that
I know what the insides

00:02:40.698 --> 00:02:42.953
of the bird looks like,
what the anatomy looks like.

00:02:42.953 --> 00:02:44.505
I feel wiser.

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:47.910
Even if I don't feel happy.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:48.703
Cleaning

00:02:48.703 --> 00:02:50.149
- So we're going to be
cleaning them a little more.

00:02:50.149 --> 00:02:51.733
You guys each have wire brushes

00:02:51.733 --> 00:02:53.968
and there's like a big
end and a small end.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.349
We're probably going to use the small end.

00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:58.498
- Do you ever like pick up road
kill and just bring it in...

00:02:58.498 --> 00:03:00.307
- Only for the museum.

00:03:00.307 --> 00:03:03.212
- I'm about to remove
the eyeball from the bird

00:03:03.212 --> 00:03:07.093
which I've been told
resembles a blueberry.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.876
- Right now, we're tossing the eyeballs

00:03:09.876 --> 00:03:12.903
and scrap bits of flesh in the meat bag.

00:03:13.457 --> 00:03:15.508
- They're gonna become
little birds in here again.

00:03:16.354 --> 00:03:17.988
I'm gonna have you get
them under the water

00:03:17.988 --> 00:03:20.772
and we're gonna turn those
skulls right side out.

00:03:20.772 --> 00:03:22.770
Pop it right through, nice and slow.

00:03:23.678 --> 00:03:25.689
It kinda becomes a little duckling again.

00:03:25.689 --> 00:03:26.481
- [Sigi] Wow.

00:03:26.481 --> 00:03:27.680
- [Allis] Now we're gonna take our soap

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.725
with our picture of the
little duckling on it.

00:03:30.432 --> 00:03:32.332
And we're gonna suds these guys up.

00:03:32.332 --> 00:03:33.633
Do you wanna suds yours up?

00:03:33.633 --> 00:03:34.405
- [Sigi] Yup.

00:03:34.405 --> 00:03:37.005
- [Allis] Get it all over on
the inside and on the outside,

00:03:37.005 --> 00:03:37.992
nice and suds.

00:03:37.992 --> 00:03:38.702
- [Sigi] So weird.

00:03:38.702 --> 00:03:39.870
Reconstructing

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.334
- What we're gonna do
now is the fill the head

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:42.838
and the eye orbits with clay.

00:03:42.838 --> 00:03:46.210
So I just pop it in there
and I pull it kinda flush.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.714
- Have a sip of coffee really quickly.

00:03:47.714 --> 00:03:48.445
- Yeah (laughs).

00:03:48.445 --> 00:03:50.253
- While I stuff my eyeballs.

00:03:50.253 --> 00:03:51.533
- See how there's wires coming out

00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:52.712
of the bottom of the legs?

00:03:52.712 --> 00:03:55.698
They go up into the little
bodies we're gonna put in.

00:03:55.698 --> 00:03:57.872
First, we're just gonna run wires

00:03:57.872 --> 00:04:00.229
up through the bottom of the feet

00:04:00.229 --> 00:04:03.012
and we're gonna go just
along our bones, okay?

00:04:03.012 --> 00:04:06.669
So we're just gonna loosely
tying it to there, okay?

00:04:06.669 --> 00:04:08.741
- I feel like I'm...

00:04:08.741 --> 00:04:11.871
a little desensitized,
there's also no more blood

00:04:11.871 --> 00:04:15.091
and guts and gore and I still have no idea

00:04:15.091 --> 00:04:17.590
how it's gonna end up being
any thing because it looks

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.829
like this right now.

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:20.414
- So me and Madison are
gonna put in your bodies

00:04:20.414 --> 00:04:22.791
and wire them and we're
gonna start sewing.

00:04:22.791 --> 00:04:25.067
Name of the game's is just
not getting feathers stuck

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:28.906
in our stitches and again, just
delicate, delicate, delicate

00:04:28.906 --> 00:04:30.532
and it doesn't need to be tight.

00:04:30.532 --> 00:04:31.974
Alright, so we're gonna fluff your bird.

00:04:31.974 --> 00:04:35.794
This dust is called chinchilla
dust, your chinchilla fluff.

00:04:35.794 --> 00:04:39.817
Basically, it's gonna help us
fluff out our little duckling

00:04:39.817 --> 00:04:41.401
and make him look happy again.

00:04:41.401 --> 00:04:43.047
- [Sigi] Oh, it's getting fluffier.

00:04:43.047 --> 00:04:44.307
- We're gonna turn on the blow dryer

00:04:44.307 --> 00:04:46.882
and this is like where the magic happens.

00:04:50.128 --> 00:04:53.392
- Awesome, so let's get his
little head right way around

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:55.018
and we're gonna get him on here.

00:04:55.018 --> 00:04:57.171
- Here is my completed bird.

00:04:57.171 --> 00:05:00.219
- It looks much happier
than he did an hour ago.

00:05:00.219 --> 00:05:02.413
- I was really freaked
out when I first got here

00:05:02.413 --> 00:05:05.258
and when we started doing
this but I'm surprised

00:05:05.258 --> 00:05:09.402
at how the day kinda progressed.

00:05:09.402 --> 00:05:14.197
- It was really, very
educational and actually

00:05:14.197 --> 00:05:15.883
more fun than I thought it was gonna be.

00:05:15.883 --> 00:05:17.384
- I liked the appreciation that I got

00:05:17.384 --> 00:05:19.579
for life for doing this.

00:05:19.579 --> 00:05:22.707
It was a very surprisingly
intimate experience.

00:05:22.707 --> 00:05:25.369
I think it's kinda
interesting and educational

00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:29.696
and I'm not sure that
veganism and taxidermy

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:33.495
are kind of mutually exclusive.

00:05:33.495 --> 00:05:35.710
- I think a lot of the
conversation today was about how,

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.221
there's a way, you know, to
treat animals really well.

00:05:38.221 --> 00:05:40.334
- It's nice to see something that had died

00:05:40.334 --> 00:05:42.162
suddenly kinda reanimated.

00:05:42.162 --> 00:05:44.011
- I started using the
word cute to describe this

00:05:44.011 --> 00:05:45.880
which I didn't think was
going to be the case.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:49.700
- Now I can say, maybe I'm vegan approved?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.980
Maybe not?

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:53.428
I don't know (laughs).

